\(\mathrm{C}_2 \mathrm{H}_5 \mathrm{OH}\) reacts with \(\mathrm{CH}_3 \mathrm{COOH}\) and gives ethylethanoate. Which is an ester and it has fruity smell.
$\begin{aligned}
\mathrm{C}_2 \mathrm{H}_5 \mathrm{OH}+\mathrm{CH}_3 \mathrm{COOH} \xrightarrow{\text{ conc. } \mathrm{H}_2 \mathrm{SO}_4} & \mathrm{CH}_3 \mathrm{COOC}_2 \mathrm{H}_5+\mathrm{H}_2 \mathrm{O} \\
& \qquad \text{ Ester } \\
& \text{ (Fruity smell) }
\end{aligned}\)$

